1
00:00:01,070 --> 00:00:03,320
Your business isn't to blame.

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:06,680
And Natsume is free to make 
and sell accessories.

3
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:12,770
But as the school, 
we have to respond somehow.

4
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:16,310
I'd hate to ask Natsume 
to take the fall, but...

5
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:21,240
We'll need you to offer flexible responses to

6
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:24,190
any parents with demands or refund requests.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,980
I understand.

8
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,940
Can a Boy-Girl Friendship Survive?

9
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:51,940
(No, It Can't!!)

10
00:01:59,590 --> 00:02:04,140
Zinnia and Where Passion Lies

11
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:01,470
We're so sorry!

12
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:04,020
I never imagined this would happen.

13
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:08,620
I swear, we just really wanted to 
promote his accessories.

14
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:12,270
So could you please apologize 
to Natsume-kun for us?

15
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:16,520
<i>Couldn't they apologize to him themselves?</i>

16
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:21,840
<i>It's pretty obvious that word 
has gotten out already.</i>

17
00:02:22,450 --> 00:02:26,810
<i>Goes to show that my support 
is as important as ever!</i>

18
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,230
<i>Who else if not me, the main wifey?</i>

19
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:34,670
<i>Gotta use my kind, tender embrace to</i>

20
00:02:34,670 --> 00:02:36,880
<i>boost Yu's trust in Himari-chan!</i>

21
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:38,340
Morning!

22
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:40,390
What is it? That hurt.

23
00:02:40,390 --> 00:02:42,960
Seriously? It's the same as usual.

24
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,180
Yeah, I guess.

25
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:50,980
<i>I guess he's still not over it.</i>

26
00:02:51,790 --> 00:02:55,030
<i>Oh well, it'll be fine!</i>

27
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:59,440
<i>This is only a small bump 
in the road towards our dream.</i>

28
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:05,010
I get why you went out of your way 
to apologize the other day.

29
00:03:05,510 --> 00:03:07,300
Here's an offer then.

30
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:11,680
Go ahead and hit me. You have that right.

31
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:16,710
That wouldn't change a thing.

32
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:20,530
Besides, I might have done the same as you

33
00:03:20,530 --> 00:03:22,640
if I ever wanted to help someone in love.

34
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:27,250
Wow, Natsu. That's unusually mature of you.

35
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:28,320
Did something happen?

36
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:29,020
I dunno.

37
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:32,960
Maybe your plan worked.

38
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,490
You're not in an awkward 
spot in band, are you?

39
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:42,080
No... I never took any orders.

40
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:46,280
What's gonna happen to the store?

41
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:50,240
We'll need to focus on damage control first.

42
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:54,270
Maybe I'll take Yu out somewhere 
over the weekend.

43
00:03:54,270 --> 00:03:56,470
That way, he can lighten up 
and get back to work.

44
00:03:56,890 --> 00:03:58,920
Are you sure that'll help?

45
00:03:59,550 --> 00:04:00,430
What do you mean?

46
00:04:00,630 --> 00:04:03,520
I mean, that must have been 
really traumatic.

47
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:05,680
Can he get over it just like that?

48
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:08,470
Don't worry about it!

49
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:12,580
Yu's never skipped 
a day of making accessories.

50
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:14,080
He'll bounce back!

51
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:18,440
When you're hurt by something you love, 
it can leave a scar that lasts forever.

52
00:04:24,610 --> 00:04:28,090
Did Makishima-kun teach you 
to rattle me like that?

53
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:30,260
This has nothing to do with Shii-kun.

54
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:34,800
But he's the one who set 
up this whole situation.

55
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:37,780
I wouldn't be surprised 
if you were in on it.

56
00:04:38,170 --> 00:04:39,340
I'd never do that!

57
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:41,420
Do you seriously think that?

58
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,490
Well, why not?

59
00:04:43,490 --> 00:04:46,980
You act like you're a ditz, 
but you're pretty calculating.

60
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,690
Like that study group!

61
00:04:48,690 --> 00:04:50,880
You pretended to be 
asleep so you could hug Yu.

62
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:53,000
I-I wasn't pretending!

63
00:04:53,850 --> 00:04:58,640
Sounds fishier the more you deny it.

64
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,900
Hey, Yu. Where have you been?

65
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:04,950
At Sasaki-sensei's.

66
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:07,600
Went to grab the accessories 
that were returned.

67
00:05:13,230 --> 00:05:16,370
My dear Yu isn't 
as weak as you are, Enocchi.

68
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:19,330
I really hate when you're 
like this, Hii-chan.

69
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,940
What should we do with them?

70
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:27,820
We can't resell them.

71
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,090
They may be damaged.

72
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:31,300
Oh...

73
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:35,520
You know, I'm still upset 
about this whole ordeal.

74
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:40,040
These were all made-to-order, 
and they agreed to the prices.

75
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,700
It can't be helped.

76
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:46,240
They're arguing that we conned them.

77
00:05:46,610 --> 00:05:47,740
<i>Something's wrong.</i>

78
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,440
<i>Yu's never this mature.</i>

79
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:53,210
<i>And it feels so gloomy.</i>

80
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:59,340
Then what's done is done. I'll get over it!

81
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:03,080
Let's go somewhere this 
weekend for a change!

82
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:04,260
Yeah, Enocchi?

83
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:06,600
S-Sure, sounds good.

84
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:09,970
Can we stop by the tea shop in the mall?

85
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:13,150
I wanna check out some summer clothes!

86
00:06:13,150 --> 00:06:15,990
Think of it as inspo 
for your next accessories.

87
00:06:15,990 --> 00:06:16,800
How's that sound?

88
00:06:18,190 --> 00:06:22,440
Actually, I'm thinking 
about quitting until we graduate.

89
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:29,640
D-Don't joke about things like that!

90
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:32,220
You could lose friends that way!

91
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:35,120
I'm not joking.

92
00:06:35,670 --> 00:06:40,280
I was wrong for acting like some 
entrepreneur as a student in the first place.

93
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:41,720
H-Hang on.

94
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:45,980
You started the store because 
you wanted to make accessories!

95
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:49,720
Sensei himself said he won't stop you 
from selling them online.

96
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:53,280
But everyone's been looking 
at me weird ever since.

97
00:06:53,910 --> 00:06:56,540
You know they've been 
talking behind my back.

98
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:58,470
Who cares? Just ignore them!

99
00:06:59,010 --> 00:07:01,600
I don't have thick skin like you.

100
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,720
Besides, why does it matter?

101
00:07:06,250 --> 00:07:08,600
I'm not quitting forever.

102
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:11,800
Just spending time to broaden 
my horizons until graduati—

103
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:13,870
Stop, stop! Let's be rational.

104
00:07:13,870 --> 00:07:15,870
Here, have some juice!

105
00:07:16,410 --> 00:07:17,460
I don't want any.

106
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:24,250
Himari, jeez...

107
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:27,000
I-It's your fault!

108
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,220
Saying you wanna quit out of nowhere.

109
00:07:29,970 --> 00:07:32,070
Like I said, only until we graduate.

110
00:07:32,810 --> 00:07:34,560
But I don't want you to quit.

111
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:36,640
I've always told you.

112
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:39,910
Your eyes shine brightest 
when you make accessories.

113
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:44,250
Come on, please?

114
00:07:44,250 --> 00:07:46,730
I'll do anything I can to help.

115
00:07:46,730 --> 00:07:50,940
So in your eyes, I'm worthless 
if I'm not making accessories?

116
00:07:52,390 --> 00:07:54,900
I didn't say that.

117
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:56,710
But it's our dream.

118
00:07:56,710 --> 00:07:59,790
Opening a store is <i>my</i> dream.

119
00:07:59,790 --> 00:08:02,600
No one else has the right 
to force me to do it!

120
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:07,680
Are you serious?

121
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:14,710
Himari!

122
00:08:14,710 --> 00:08:15,340
Hii-chan!

123
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,310
Fine, I get it.

124
00:08:27,310 --> 00:08:28,650
Have it your way!

125
00:08:45,660 --> 00:08:47,420
Himari, dinner's ready.

126
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:50,110
Why haven't you changed yet?

127
00:08:52,110 --> 00:08:53,980
Upset about something?

128
00:08:54,260 --> 00:08:57,510
Yu's apparently quitting 
accessories until we graduate.

129
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:00,440
Let me guess...

130
00:09:00,810 --> 00:09:03,690
You pushed Yu-kun too hard about

131
00:09:03,690 --> 00:09:06,780
his next piece when he was at a low point?

132
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:09,280
Because...!

133
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:17,060
What if Yu really lost his passion?

134
00:09:17,450 --> 00:09:19,450
Himari, you're finally catching on.

135
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:24,550
Good job. You did the right thing.

136
00:09:25,450 --> 00:09:27,220
When I told you to stop lying,

137
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:29,770
I meant be honest with yourself.

138
00:09:30,310 --> 00:09:34,910
So it's good that you told Yu-kun 
how you really felt.

139
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:37,330
Then Yu will understand, right?

140
00:09:39,890 --> 00:09:41,120
Who knows?

141
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:45,310
Right now, there's nothing else we can do.

142
00:09:45,910 --> 00:09:48,430
Yu-kun will have to 
overcome this on his own.

143
00:09:49,750 --> 00:09:53,840
After all, creativity
is about facing the self.

144
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:58,600
Yu-kun tried to reach 
his goal, and as a result,

145
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:01,510
he got shot down 
by the ill intent of others.

146
00:10:02,410 --> 00:10:06,760
But that's inevitable 
if he wants to pursue this path.

147
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:10,580
Can he laugh and shrug it off

148
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:14,040
when someone unfairly taints his work?

149
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,100
That's the crossroads he's at.

150
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:19,760
Only those who overcome 
this can move forward.

151
00:10:20,330 --> 00:10:24,310
No words of encouragement 
or solace can do that for him.

152
00:10:25,690 --> 00:10:28,230
Himari, what can you do right now?

153
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:31,910
Didn't you just say 
there's nothing I can do?

154
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:35,430
Sure, Yu-kun has to help himself back up.

155
00:10:36,190 --> 00:10:39,040
But you have your own role as his partner.

156
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:45,020
As Yu-kun's best friend, 
you've been spoiled by his kindness.

157
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:48,160
But when it comes to his accessories, 
it's been the opposite.

158
00:10:48,490 --> 00:10:50,920
Yu-kun's been spoiled by you, Himari.

159
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:52,620
What do you mean?

160
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:55,100
Think back to when You 
announced new releases.

161
00:10:55,350 --> 00:10:57,920
Either you or Sakura-kun laid 
the groundwork.

162
00:10:58,680 --> 00:11:02,640
Like a playground frozen in time, Yu-kun's
 talent was nurtured in a closed environment.

163
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:04,240
He was vulnerable to external exposure.

164
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:09,350
Before long, Yu-kun would need to
 practice dealing with the outside world.

165
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:12,920
Feeling defeated, Yu-kun tried 
to retreat back to his playground.

166
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:15,090
But you pushed back and told him no.

167
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:18,570
As his partner, you showed him the way out.

168
00:11:19,690 --> 00:11:22,320
Now, it's Yu-kun's turn to answer the call.

169
00:11:22,970 --> 00:11:26,180
Himari, if you truly share 
destinies with Yu-kun,

170
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:29,590
what can you do for him 
now as his best friend?

171
00:11:34,090 --> 00:11:36,470
About yesterday, that was my bad.

172
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:38,760
I took it too far.

173
00:11:40,010 --> 00:11:42,480
Did Enocchi and Sakura-san tell you that?

174
00:11:43,030 --> 00:11:45,760
No, I know I was in the wrong.

175
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:47,860
Besides, you've worked so hard for me—

176
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:49,330
I'm not talking about that.

177
00:11:49,330 --> 00:11:50,990
What about your work?

178
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:55,720
That's a done deal.

179
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:58,560
I'm quitting until we graduate.

180
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:05,480
If that's what you really want, fine.

181
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:07,930
I'll quit being your best friend then.

182
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:11,600
If you won't make accessories anymore,

183
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:13,290
you and I are only acquaintances.

184
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:15,350
A-Are you for real?

185
00:12:15,350 --> 00:12:17,250
Why are you getting so upset about this?

186
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:20,280
Sure, I was wrong 
for what I said yesterday, but—

187
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:23,610
But you're still quitting, right?

188
00:12:24,470 --> 00:12:25,280
Well...

189
00:12:26,740 --> 00:12:28,370
Opening your store isn't just your dream.

190
00:12:28,370 --> 00:12:30,770
It's been mine for a long time, too!

191
00:12:30,770 --> 00:12:33,440
You can't just decide to quit on your own!

192
00:12:34,050 --> 00:12:37,440
Sure, I have fun with you,
and I'd like to stay best friends.

193
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:41,080
But if you're gonna stomp on my dreams,

194
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,990
then we're not friends.

195
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:49,240
I refuse to play nice like Enocchi.

196
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:52,610
Sorry, but I'm moving forward without you.

197
00:12:54,860 --> 00:12:58,420
You're one to talk. 
You tried to quit, too.

198
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:03,600
<i>After that...</i>

199
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:05,920
<i>The weekend came and went without Himari.</i>

200
00:13:06,810 --> 00:13:09,160
Himari-chan! Whatcha up to today?

201
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:13,520
I actually have plans today, sorry!

202
00:13:17,990 --> 00:13:18,700
Yu-kun.

203
00:13:21,690 --> 00:13:23,150
Natsume

204
00:13:23,150 --> 00:13:24,890
There, Enomoto-san!

205
00:13:24,890 --> 00:13:25,610
Got it!

206
00:13:25,610 --> 00:13:28,280
What? How?

207
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:30,040
I'll get you this time!

208
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:34,800
Enomoto-san, you gotta learn to aim.

209
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,770
Aim? How do I do that?!

210
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:38,880
So your screen stays stable.

211
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:41,530
I can't figure it out!

212
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:43,630
<i>She's so clueless.</i>

213
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:49,230
I took down one person, 
so I must be getting better.

214
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,260
This is so much fun.

215
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:54,040
Yeah, it sure is.

216
00:13:57,430 --> 00:14:00,270
Yu-kun, you're not a very good liar.

217
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:04,580
I'm not lying. I have fun 
playing games with you.

218
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:07,240
Not as much as when 
you're making accessories.

219
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:10,410
That was until last week.

220
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,950
Who wants to make accessories just 
to go through all that?

221
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:13,840
You're lying.

222
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:18,530
You wouldn't be able to spend two years 
with Hii-chan if you were that soft.

223
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:20,990
That's none of your business.

224
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:22,420
Sure it is.

225
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:25,800
I decided to be number one. For both of you.

226
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:29,760
What a drag.

227
00:14:30,930 --> 00:14:32,760
I said, "What a drag."

228
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:35,820
What gives you the right to judge the
relationship between me and Himari?

229
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:38,040
I hate how you stick your nose 
in other people's business.

230
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:44,280
I'm glad you feel comfortable 
enough to say stuff like that.

231
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:46,730
It's like I'm getting closer to Hii-chan.

232
00:14:47,170 --> 00:14:49,280
You've gotta be kidding!

233
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:52,330
I'm pretty sure I just said 
something really messed up.

234
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:56,650
Like I said, it's obvious when you're lying.

235
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:59,120
So it's no use.

236
00:15:01,470 --> 00:15:03,840
Can I ask you something?

237
00:15:12,390 --> 00:15:13,070
Here.

238
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:15,500
Who does it look like I made this for?

239
00:15:17,810 --> 00:15:18,590
Hii-chan.

240
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:19,480
I figured.

241
00:15:20,890 --> 00:15:23,260
In that moment, I didn't feel anything.

242
00:15:24,530 --> 00:15:27,080
Even though I sacrificed sleep to make it.

243
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:29,820
I didn't even feel mad.

244
00:15:30,650 --> 00:15:31,510
So I asked myself.

245
00:15:31,510 --> 00:15:34,940
What's the passion behind my accessories?

246
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:39,000
Why in the world am I making them?

247
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:40,880
That was when I realized...

248
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:46,930
I was only making accessories 
so Himari would keep me around.

249
00:15:48,170 --> 00:15:50,810
So I wouldn't lose the first 
person who understood what I loved.

250
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:54,680
So I wouldn't lose my first best friend.

251
00:15:56,440 --> 00:16:00,230
I was just using people's 
love lives as a stepping stone.

252
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:02,740
All to make accessories for myself.

253
00:16:03,730 --> 00:16:06,440
I felt so disgusted with myself...

254
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:11,840
For thinking love was so pure...

255
00:16:12,830 --> 00:16:15,020
For thinking my feelings were genuine.

256
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:18,410
I couldn't have been more wrong.

257
00:16:19,610 --> 00:16:22,080
That's why I wanted to 
quit making accessories.

258
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:28,280
Otherwise, it wouldn't be right 
to the craft or to customers.

259
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:29,680
Yu-kun.

260
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:34,860
Get over yourself!

261
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:38,480
I think you're overthinking it.

262
00:16:38,870 --> 00:16:40,770
Loosen up a little.

263
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:42,820
Loosen up?

264
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:47,850
It'd be nice if I could 
be as earnest as you.

265
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:50,940
But I wouldn't have so much doubt 
if that were the case.

266
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:54,120
Me, earnest? How?

267
00:16:55,220 --> 00:16:58,030
I mean, you're always 
helping your family's store.

268
00:16:58,360 --> 00:16:59,950
You work really hard in band.

269
00:17:00,670 --> 00:17:01,770
And you help me.

270
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:05,630
I kinda hate helping at my family's store.

271
00:17:06,390 --> 00:17:09,530
I only joined band
because my friend asked me to.

272
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:12,090
That's why I skip practice 
sometimes, like today.

273
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:14,340
I'm not earnest at all.

274
00:17:14,770 --> 00:17:17,850
And when you and Hii-chan are fighting,

275
00:17:18,090 --> 00:17:20,880
I like having you all to myself.

276
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:24,560
I'm human, just like everyone else.

277
00:17:26,020 --> 00:17:30,310
Yu-kun, is it that weird I don't give 
up when you turn me down?

278
00:17:30,310 --> 00:17:32,400
H-Honestly, yeah.

279
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:33,800
I can't help it.

280
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:37,050
I like you, Yu-kun.

281
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:42,120
My world shines brighter 
just hearing you say my name.

282
00:17:44,010 --> 00:17:44,850
That's the fifth time.

283
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:47,920
I-I can't, sorry.

284
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:52,460
Who cares if you make 
accessories for Hii-chan?

285
00:17:54,210 --> 00:17:57,980
If that makes other 
people happy, then great.

286
00:17:57,980 --> 00:18:01,890
If it happens to ruin someone's love life, 
how's that your problem?

287
00:18:03,550 --> 00:18:06,810
I wouldn't mind if you 
quit making accessories.

288
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:10,330
If you find something else 
you wanna do, I'd join you.

289
00:18:10,330 --> 00:18:13,690
If that lifts your spirits, 
it'll make me happy, too.

290
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:15,810
Which one do you choose?

291
00:18:16,150 --> 00:18:17,080
Me or Hii-chan?

292
00:18:20,310 --> 00:18:23,100
<i>If I could just quit making accessories,</i>

293
00:18:23,650 --> 00:18:25,490
<i>if I could just choose 
Enomoto-san like this...</i>

294
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:28,140
<i>I'm sure that would be a happy life.</i>

295
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:32,560
<i>But it'd be a life without Himari.</i>

296
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:36,990
Enomoto-san, I'm sorry.

297
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:39,890
That's okay.

298
00:18:40,410 --> 00:18:42,830
I know I'm a good ten laps behind.

299
00:18:43,350 --> 00:18:46,440
But I think I just closed the gap to seven!

300
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:48,550
You're so optimistic.

301
00:18:49,090 --> 00:18:49,970
Ready?

302
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:52,240
Let's go.

303
00:18:58,950 --> 00:18:59,650
Himari...

304
00:18:59,910 --> 00:19:02,370
No outsiders allowed!

305
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:06,080
Outsider? Come on, I apologized.

306
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:08,700
But you're not making accessories, right?

307
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:11,540
You better show some sincerity 
if you want forgiveness.

308
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,240
Sincerity?

309
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:15,960
First, a monthly "Thank 
You Himari-sama Day."

310
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:20,560
You have to do whatever I want 
for a day every—

311
00:19:21,170 --> 00:19:23,960
Hii-chan, don't you have 
something to tell Yu-kun?

312
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:26,560
Ow, ow. Okay, fine.

313
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:32,720
Yu, you see, I...

314
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:36,000
I lied about going to Tokyo.

315
00:19:36,210 --> 00:19:37,240
I'm sorry!

316
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:38,950
After all this time?

317
00:19:46,730 --> 00:19:47,400
It's fine.

318
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:50,480
Whether that part was true or not,

319
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:53,550
it doesn't change the fact that 
you're the most important to me.

320
00:19:57,750 --> 00:19:58,840
What the—

321
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:00,040
What are you doing?

322
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:04,100
I-I'll go get a towel!

323
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:07,800
Even if you say you're quitting,

324
00:20:08,350 --> 00:20:11,520
I still love watching you make accessories.

325
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:14,210
More than anything in the world!

326
00:20:15,430 --> 00:20:18,880
So let me know when you wanna start again.

327
00:20:19,330 --> 00:20:21,160
I'll be waiting here forever.

328
00:20:22,790 --> 00:20:26,180
This taught me... that's my answer.

329
00:20:27,330 --> 00:20:30,320
That's not why I said I wanted to quit.

330
00:20:32,110 --> 00:20:32,680
I realized.

331
00:20:33,250 --> 00:20:37,110
The reason why I made accessories 
all this time was to make you happy.

332
00:20:37,850 --> 00:20:41,510
I felt so guilty towards 
the customers, I panicked.

333
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:42,890
I'm sorry.

334
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:50,310
Bwa-ha!

335
00:20:50,800 --> 00:20:55,480
Gosh, Yu! You really just 
can't get enough of me!

336
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:58,800
I basically <i>have</i> to forgive you 
when you put it like that!

337
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:04,280
You want <i>that</i> badly to make up 
with the beautiful Himari-chan?

338
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:06,360
Man, you're talkative.

339
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:07,750
<i>Well duh!</i>

340
00:21:07,750 --> 00:21:09,820
<i>Even I'm blushing over that.</i>

341
00:21:10,010 --> 00:21:10,530
Take this!

342
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:18,760
If you like me so much, 
wanna actually go out?

343
00:21:21,170 --> 00:21:22,950
Anyone but you, Himari!

344
00:21:22,950 --> 00:21:24,840
Bwa-ha!

345
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:27,280
<i>And so, the rainy season ended.</i>

346
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:32,360
<i>And my second summer break
 of high school was drawing near...</i>

347
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:38,650
No way.

348
00:21:38,890 --> 00:21:40,820
Shinji-kun, you're the one picking me up?

349
00:21:41,010 --> 00:21:42,800
My brother's busy today.

350
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:44,060
I'll take your luggage.

351
00:21:44,540 --> 00:21:46,500
Aww, thanks.

352
00:21:46,500 --> 00:21:47,330
Why the sudden trip?

353
00:21:47,780 --> 00:21:49,890
You're not here to see Rin-chan, are you?

354
00:21:49,890 --> 00:21:51,850
Of course not!

355
00:21:51,850 --> 00:21:56,320
I came to scold that junior 
who dragged my name, that's all.

356
00:21:56,780 --> 00:21:57,800
Is that so?

357
00:21:58,030 --> 00:22:00,510
Mind if I get in on that?

358
00:22:00,830 --> 00:22:01,790
Kureha-san.

359
00:23:35,300 --> 00:23:40,020
Love's Chocolate Cosmos

